{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Exploring Open Math Assessment Data\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook walks through a first look at two publicly available math assessment datasets\n",
    "hosted on [Open Math Insights (OMI)](https://rkn2.github.io/open-math-insights/):\n",
    "\n",
    "- **NAEP** (National Assessment of Educational Progress) — U.S. national and state-level\n",
    "  average math scale scores for grades 4 and 8, 2003–2024.\n",
    "- **PISA** (Programme for International Student Assessment) — international math scores for\n",
    "  15-year-olds across 80+ countries, 2003–2022.\n",
    "\n",
    "You'll learn how to:\n",
    "1. Load CSV data directly from a URL\n",
    "2. Inspect structure and summary statistics\n",
    "3. Visualize trends over time\n",
    "4. Run a basic clustering analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "**No install required** — this notebook runs as-is in Google Colab."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.rcParams.update({\n",
    "    \"figure.figsize\": (10, 5),\n",
    "    \"axes.spines.top\": False,\n",
    "    \"axes.spines.right\": False,\n",
    "    \"font.size\": 11,\n",
    "})"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Load the NAEP dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "We load directly from the OMI Data Depot's raw CSV on GitHub. The NAEP dataset has\n",
    "132 rows covering average math scale scores by year, grade, and jurisdiction."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "NAEP_URL = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rkn2/open-math-insights/main/public/data/naep_math_scale_scores.csv\"\n",
    "\n",
    "naep = pd.read_csv(NAEP_URL)\n",
    "print(f\"Shape: {naep.shape}\")\n",
    "naep.head(10)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "naep.dtypes"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "naep.describe()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### What's in this dataset?\n",
    "\n",
    "| Column | Meaning |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| `year` | Assessment year (2003–2024) |\n",
    "| `grade` | Grade level tested (4 or 8) |\n",
    "| `jurisdiction` | Two-letter code: NP = National Public, plus CA, FL, MA, NY, TX |\n",
    "| `jurisdiction_label` | Full name |\n",
    "| `avg_scale_score` | Average NAEP math scale score (0–500 scale) |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"Jurisdictions:\", naep[\"jurisdiction\"].unique())\n",
    "print(\"Grades:\", naep[\"grade\"].unique())\n",
    "print(\"Year range:\", naep[\"year\"].min(), \"–\", naep[\"year\"].max())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Visualize NAEP trends over time"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 5), sharey=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "for ax, grade in zip(axes, [4, 8]):\n",
    "    subset = naep[naep[\"grade\"] == grade]\n",
    "    for jur in subset[\"jurisdiction\"].unique():\n",
    "        data = subset[subset[\"jurisdiction\"] == jur]\n",
    "        label = data[\"jurisdiction_label\"].iloc[0]\n",
    "        style = {\"linewidth\": 2.5, \"marker\": \"o\", \"markersize\": 4}\n",
    "        if jur == \"NP\":\n",
    "            style.update({\"linewidth\": 3, \"color\": \"#1e3a5f\", \"zorder\": 10})\n",
    "        ax.plot(data[\"year\"], data[\"avg_scale_score\"], label=label, **style)\n",
    "    ax.set_title(f\"Grade {grade}\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel(\"Year\")\n",
    "    ax.set_ylabel(\"Avg Scale Score\")\n",
    "    ax.legend(fontsize=8, loc=\"lower left\")\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.suptitle(\"NAEP Math Scale Scores by Jurisdiction\", fontweight=\"bold\", fontsize=13)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### What to notice\n",
    "\n",
    "- Most jurisdictions show a dip after 2019 — consistent with widely reported pandemic-era\n",
    "  score declines.\n",
    "- Massachusetts (MA) consistently scores above the national average.\n",
    "- The national trend for grade 4 peaked around 2011–2013 and has been flat or declining since."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Load the PISA dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "PISA tests 15-year-olds internationally. This dataset has average math scores for\n",
    "80+ countries across assessment cycles from 2003 to 2022."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "PISA_URL = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rkn2/open-math-insights/main/public/data/pisa_math_scores.csv\"\n",
    "\n",
    "pisa = pd.read_csv(PISA_URL)\n",
    "print(f\"Shape: {pisa.shape}\")\n",
    "pisa.head(10)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "pisa.describe()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(f\"Countries: {pisa['entity'].nunique()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Year range: {pisa['year'].min()} – {pisa['year'].max()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nCountries with data in every cycle:\")\n",
    "\n",
    "all_years = set(pisa[\"year\"].unique())\n",
    "complete = pisa.groupby(\"entity\")[\"year\"].apply(lambda y: set(y) == all_years)\n",
    "print(\", \".join(sorted(complete[complete].index)))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Explore PISA score distributions"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 5))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Distribution of scores across all country-years\n",
    "axes[0].hist(pisa[\"pisa_math_all_average\"], bins=30, color=\"#2563eb\", edgecolor=\"white\")\n",
    "axes[0].set_xlabel(\"PISA Math Score\")\n",
    "axes[0].set_ylabel(\"Count (country-years)\")\n",
    "axes[0].set_title(\"Distribution of PISA Math Scores\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "axes[0].axvline(pisa[\"pisa_math_all_average\"].mean(), color=\"#dc2626\", linestyle=\"--\",\n",
    "               label=f\"Mean: {pisa['pisa_math_all_average'].mean():.0f}\")\n",
    "axes[0].legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Scores over time for a few countries\n",
    "highlights = [\"United States\", \"Japan\", \"Finland\", \"Brazil\", \"Singapore\"]\n",
    "for country in highlights:\n",
    "    d = pisa[pisa[\"entity\"] == country].sort_values(\"year\")\n",
    "    if len(d) > 0:\n",
    "        axes[1].plot(d[\"year\"], d[\"pisa_math_all_average\"], marker=\"o\", label=country)\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[1].set_xlabel(\"Year\")\n",
    "axes[1].set_ylabel(\"PISA Math Score\")\n",
    "axes[1].set_title(\"PISA Trends: Selected Countries\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "axes[1].legend(fontsize=9)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Basic feature exploration\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's look at the PISA data more quantitatively: which countries improved the most,\n",
    "which declined, and how spread out are the scores within each assessment year?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Countries with both an early (<=2006) and a late (>=2018) score\n",
    "early = pisa[pisa[\"year\"] <= 2006].groupby(\"entity\")[\"pisa_math_all_average\"].mean()\n",
    "late = pisa[pisa[\"year\"] >= 2018].groupby(\"entity\")[\"pisa_math_all_average\"].mean()\n",
    "change = (late - early).dropna().sort_values()\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 8))\n",
    "colors = [\"#dc2626\" if v < 0 else \"#16a34a\" for v in change]\n",
    "ax.barh(change.index, change.values, color=colors)\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"Change in PISA Math Score (late avg − early avg)\")\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"Score Change: Early (≤2006) vs Late (≥2018) PISA Cycles\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "ax.axvline(0, color=\"#64748b\", linewidth=0.8)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Spread of scores within each year\n",
    "yearly_stats = pisa.groupby(\"year\")[\"pisa_math_all_average\"].agg([\"mean\", \"std\", \"min\", \"max\"])\n",
    "yearly_stats[\"range\"] = yearly_stats[\"max\"] - yearly_stats[\"min\"]\n",
    "yearly_stats"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Simple clustering: grouping countries by performance trajectory\n",
    "\n",
    "Can we find natural groupings of countries based on how their PISA scores evolved?\n",
    "We'll pivot the data into a country × year matrix and run K-Means clustering."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.cluster import KMeans\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "\n",
    "# Pivot: countries as rows, years as columns\n",
    "pivot = pisa.pivot_table(index=\"entity\", columns=\"year\",\n",
    "                         values=\"pisa_math_all_average\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Keep only countries with data in at least 4 cycles\n",
    "pivot_clean = pivot.dropna(thresh=4)\n",
    "# Fill remaining gaps with row mean for clustering\n",
    "pivot_filled = pivot_clean.T.fillna(pivot_clean.mean(axis=1)).T\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Countries included: {len(pivot_filled)}\")\n",
    "pivot_filled.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
    "X = scaler.fit_transform(pivot_filled)\n",
    "\n",
    "kmeans = KMeans(n_clusters=4, random_state=42, n_init=10)\n",
    "pivot_filled[\"cluster\"] = kmeans.fit_predict(X)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Cluster sizes:\")\n",
    "print(pivot_filled[\"cluster\"].value_counts().sort_index())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(14, 10), sharey=True)\n",
    "cluster_colors = [\"#2563eb\", \"#16a34a\", \"#dc2626\", \"#9333ea\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "for cluster_id, ax in enumerate(axes.flat):\n",
    "    members = pivot_filled[pivot_filled[\"cluster\"] == cluster_id]\n",
    "    year_cols = [c for c in members.columns if c != \"cluster\"]\n",
    "    for _, row in members.iterrows():\n",
    "        ax.plot(year_cols, row[year_cols], alpha=0.3, color=cluster_colors[cluster_id])\n",
    "    # cluster mean\n",
    "    ax.plot(year_cols, members[year_cols].mean(), linewidth=2.5,\n",
    "            color=cluster_colors[cluster_id], label=f\"Cluster mean\")\n",
    "    ax.set_title(f\"Cluster {cluster_id} ({len(members)} countries)\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel(\"Year\")\n",
    "    ax.set_ylabel(\"PISA Math Score\")\n",
    "    ax.legend(fontsize=8)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.suptitle(\"Country Clusters by PISA Math Trajectory\", fontweight=\"bold\", fontsize=13)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Which countries are in each cluster?\n",
    "for c in sorted(pivot_filled[\"cluster\"].unique()):\n",
    "    countries = sorted(pivot_filled[pivot_filled[\"cluster\"] == c].index)\n",
    "    print(f\"\\nCluster {c}: {', '.join(countries)}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Interpreting the clusters\n",
    "\n",
    "K-Means is finding groups based on both **level** (high vs. low scores) and **trajectory**\n",
    "(improving, stable, or declining). A few things to keep in mind:\n",
    "\n",
    "- The cluster count (4) was chosen for readability, not from a rigorous elbow analysis —\n",
    "  try changing `n_clusters` and see how the groupings shift.\n",
    "- Countries with missing years were gap-filled with their row mean, which smooths the\n",
    "  trajectory. For serious analysis, you'd handle missingness more carefully.\n",
    "- These are **descriptive** groupings, not causal explanations. "Cluster 0 countries have\n",
    "  high scores" does not tell you *why*."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Next steps\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Notebook 02** compares NAEP and PISA side-by-side — what you can and can't infer\n",
    "  across the two systems.\n",
    "- The [OMI Data Depot](https://rkn2.github.io/open-math-insights/data-depot) has\n",
    "  additional datasets, including ASSISTments student-level data.\n",
    "- The [Researcher Guide](https://rkn2.github.io/open-math-insights/researcher-guide)\n",
    "  covers de-identification, repository choice, and data preparation."
   ]
  }
